 ## Overview
-Hash Grids map continuous 3D vertex positions to discrete bucket indices in a hash table using a multiplicative hash with prime constants [S1, unofficial]. This method enables sparse feature extraction by storing attributes only at hashed locations, avoiding the memory overhead of dense grids. It differs from its parent [Sparse structures](5-sparse-structures.md) by using a flat hash table rather than hierarchical tree structures, and from siblings like [Compact pointer tree](844-compact-pointer-tree.md) by relying on direct hashing rather than pointer compression for spatial indexing.
